link_dpms.c, above `void link_restart_all_streams_for_link(struct dc_link *link)`:
cinemaONE test (dc_hpo_frl_retrain_in_place=2, 2026-09-27): every stream on
the link off and on again through stream updates, as
link_set_all_streams_dpms_off_for_link() does for the first half. The "on"
runs the normal enable path -- link training, LTS:P waiting for FRL_Start,
then the stream -- without a mode set of the timing generator.

link_hdmi_frl.c, above `static int frl_retrain_in_place;`:
  2  every stream on the link off and on again (stream updates with
     dpms_off), whose "on" trains the link and waits for FRL_Start before
     the stream starts; no training of its own, no detect. With 1 the
     VRROOM never set FRL_Start while the stream kept sending video.

